{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CgoaYci4hoD5SGW8DoqU2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ajv1kTrThSsZVdDE1Q5Cmr","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"fix_prompt":"# Repair plan for /playwright/playwright:`<startup>`\n\n## 1. Diagnosis — why the set fails\n\nThe failing \"test\" is not an assertion failure. `<startup>` is Playwright's\nsynthetic entry for a **global startup error**: the run dies before any spec\nexecutes, so the failure group body is empty and `tests/integration/frontend-home.spec.ts`\nnever runs.\n\nThe cause is structural, not behavioural:\n\n- `tests/playwright.config.ts` declares a `webServer` with\n  `command: 'docker compose up --build frontend'`, `cwd: '..'`, and waits on\n  `http://127.0.0.1:${port}` (port derived from `process.cwd()`), passing\n  `FRONTEND_PORT` and `COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME`.\n- `docker-compose.yaml` defines exactly one service, `frontend`, with\n  `build.context: ./services/frontend` and port mapping\n  `\"${FRONTEND_PORT:-3000}:3000\"` — i.e. the app must listen on **3000 inside\n  the container**.\n- **`services/` does not exist in the workspace at all.** There is no\n  `services/frontend`, no Dockerfile, no Next.js app. `docker compose up --build\n  frontend` therefore fails immediately on the missing build context, the\n  `webServer` url is never served, and Playwright aborts the run at startup.\n\n`docs/architecture/architecture.yaml` and `CLAUDE.md` confirm the intent: the\n`frontend` service lives at `services/frontend`, language `typescript`,\nframeworks `next.js` + `react`, with a `quality_gate.code` entry\n`typescript -> services/frontend/tsconfig.json`. So the repair is to **build the\nmissing production service**, entirely inside the declared edit root\n`services/frontend`. Nothing under `tests/`, `docs/`, `true-bdd/` or\n`docker-compose.yaml` needs to change, and nothing outside `services/frontend`\nis required.\n\n## 2. The contract 